# Line endings matter for the installers, in both directions.
#
# Windows batch files need CRLF: cmd.exe mis-parses a multi-line `if (...)`
# block in an LF-only .bat. Shell scripts need LF: bash fails with
# "\r: command not found" if a Windows checkout gives them CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.sh  text eol=lf
